Reason: The provided class `FlowableEmpty` is a trivial, stateless singleton that immediately completes without emitting any items. Its behavior involves only a single method call to `EmptySubscription.complete`, which has negligible computational work. Benchmarking such a no-op or near-no-op implementation with JMH would not yield meaningful performance insights and would primarily measure framework overhead rather than the class's own logic. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this code is unnecessary.